--- body ---
## Context
Two probe defects met in one test-doctor consultation on 2026-11-12. Both
return an all-clear that cannot be told from "I could not look".

1. `scripts/gate_traces.py collect --project climate-finance-het --days 28`
   printed `climate-finance-het: 0 foreground gate runs in 28d (0 sessions,
   0 background, 0 unpaired, 0 unreadable)`. The same call with the absolute
   project path found 652 runs in 503 sessions. `--project` is a path
   (`project_directories` encodes it into a trace-directory name); a bare
   name matches no directory and the tool reports zero instead of failing.
   `skills/test-doctor/SKILL.md` § Examination writes `--project <project>`,
   which invites the name.
2. `scripts/gate_profile.py profile .test_durations.json --workers 16` read a
   record last written 2026-07-27, three and a half months old, without a
   word; it still listed two 236 s tests the selection had since dropped,
   and its lower bound (236.6 s) described a suite that no longer exists.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `gate_traces.py` exits non-zero with a message naming the encoded
      directory it looked for when `--project` resolves to no trace
      directory (0 sessions), on every subcommand that takes `--project`.
- [ ] The test-doctor Examination lines say the argument is the project's
      absolute path.
- [ ] `gate_profile.py profile` prints the record's age (file mtime, or a
      timestamp inside the record when there is one) and warns past a
      threshold (suggest 14 days); `compare` does the same for both inputs.
- [ ] A red test for each, from the motivating case.
